A||||3||ezsurf||Turn Stalk?||||5||
Z||000000||ezsurf||10-08-2001||10:08 AM||||I've never had this problem before, so I'm not sure what it is.  When I give a left turn signal the blinker flashes normally.  When I give a right turn signal, it lights up but does not flash.  I don't know if it's the turn stalk, flasher capacitor or who knows what.  Anyone had this problem and figured out how to fix it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||10-08-2001||10:19 AM||||You most likely have a blown bulb either in front, rear or side.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||10-08-2001||10:24 AM||||Yep. Like Phil said. It is designed that way to let you know about the blown bulb.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ezsurf||10-08-2001||10:42 AM||||Thanks for the info, I'll check it out.  For once it sounds like an easy fix.  (I can't believe I just said that!)||||reg||14
